-- defect: a `Dict` keyed by a COMPOSITE type. A Sky `Dict k v` is a Go
-- `map[string]v` — the key is stringified on the way in and decoded on the way
-- out — and `fmt.Sprintf("%v", key)` is NOT injective on a tuple: ( "a b", "c" )
-- and ( "a", "b c" ) both render `{a b c}`, so two distinct keys collide and one
-- entry is silently lost. No decoder can recover the original, which is why this
-- is unfixable at the runtime layer rather than merely unimplemented.
--
-- The key is written through the alias `Coord`, so this file also pins that
-- alias expansion happens BEFORE the check (`sig::World::expand`) — a bypass
-- via `type alias Coord = ( Int, Int )` would otherwise be trivial.
--
-- rust: reject [E2008] — check-time rejection with source context.
-- oracle: ACCEPTS this program and panics at runtime (`rt.Dict: unsupported key
-- type`, classified `UnsupportedDictKey` by `runtime-go/rt/panic_recover.go`).
-- This is a DELIBERATE Sky-rust divergence in the strict direction: a panic out
-- of code that passed `sky check` violates "if it compiles, it works"
-- (AGENTS.md), so the checker refuses the program instead. Never "reconcile"
-- this by relaxing the Rust side.
--
-- ACCEPTED TWIN — `rust/crates/ty/tests/dict_key.rs`
-- (`accepts_every_supported_key_type` + `accepts_key_polymorphic_signature`)
-- checks the same program with each of the five supported key types, and with a
-- key-polymorphic `Dict k v` helper. Without those, this file would be satisfied
-- by a checker that rejects everything.
module Main exposing (main)

import Sky.Core.Dict as Dict exposing (Dict)
import Sky.Core.Prelude exposing (..)
import Std.Log exposing (println)


type alias Coord =
    ( Int, Int )


grid : Dict Coord String
grid =
    Dict.insert ( 1, 2 ) "wall" Dict.empty


main =
    println (String.fromInt (Dict.size grid))
